  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1202 AM CDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nNext week will be hot and generally dry for our area with daily \nhighs 8-12 degrees above normal. The strong upper level high will be \nover the New Mexico/Texas border Sunday-Tuesday, and then slowly \nmigrate west toward the New Mexico/Arizona border by Thursday-\nFriday. The hottest days look to be Sunday through Tuesday, with the \nhigh in closer proximity and the 850mb thermal ridge the strongest. \nExpect highs to be 104-107 across the Concho Valley and 105-110 in \nthe Big Country. Our southern counties will have highs mostly 100-\n103 degrees. Anticipate the need for additional Heat Advisories for \nour northern and central counties, and some locations north of I-20 \nmay approach Extreme Heat Warning criteria. By Thursday and Friday, \nexpect highs to be in the upper 90s/around 100 in our southern \ncounties, and 100-105 degrees farther north across the rest of our \narea.   \n\nWith weak northerly flow aloft around the eastern side of the \naforementioned high in the midweek time frame, some of the medium \nrange models hint at a possibility for a few showers and \nthunderstorms to develop along a surface trough as it moves south \ninto our area Wednesday night and Thursday. The possibility looks \nremote at this time, however.",
